    "turn_text": "Zero. So we got like four hours to lunch. You know what I mean? And we have a training regime. Everyone goes out. They're training. I'm sitting there with my tasking commander and these guys. And we're just dunkins in there. And we just started talking with him right now. I mean, an unclassified level. Just talk, talk, talk, talk. And then they pack up. They go back to Hollywood or whatever. We finish our training five weeks later, something like that. And I get a call from a guy named Tom Brown, who unfortunately just died. retired, Admiral, at that time he was a captain, he's a Commodore, very good man, friend of mine. He just last month, April, he died, I don't know, a lot of friends have died. So he calls me over. And it's not a good thing, whether the guy who's in charge of the entire coast of the seal teams calls you over to his office. I mean, to talk to you personally. Now I did a very a very specialized mission set in the Horn of Africa. So I had a much more personal relationship with this guy than you normally do between the E8 and the 06. But so we, I mean, we knew each other, you know, because I reported almost directly, it was a weird thing. But anyway, so I knew you're right. It calls me over, he's like, Hey, I know it was been to you guys, you know, they want you to be in a movie. They want you to do it. And I was like, Hey, color, you can't order me to be in a movie. He's like, Hey, But you know, you're right, I can't. I'm like, OK, well, thanks for the talk. And he's like, oh, this is where this guy was. He goes, oh, why don't you go home and ask Sarah Janie about it? And I was like, OK, sure. It's a weird conversation. But so I go home and I'm better. I'm like, hey, honey, remember those guys that came out from Hollywood, they want me to be in that movie. And she was like, Well, what'd you tell them? I said, no, I'm not being there. Movie? No, I'm not an actor. I'm a seal. Not happening. She's like, oh, okay. Well, maybe if you did that movie, your kids don't know why you spent so many years away from the home.",
